{
  "about": [
    "Model prices Foreman uses to estimate cost. USD per 1M tokens, Standard tier, public API list prices.",
    "These are API-equivalent estimates: a Claude or ChatGPT subscription is billed differently, and tool/container fees are not included.",
    "To update: change or add entries under 'models' and set 'pricingDate' to the day you checked the sources. Keep the file valid JSON.",
    "Per model: model (id as the CLI reports it, lower case, without a date suffix or [1m]), provider ('claude' or 'codex'), input, output,",
    "and optionally: aliases (other ids with the same price), cachedInput (cache reads), cacheWrite (5-minute cache writes),",
    "cacheWriteLong (1-hour cache writes), longContext (true when every token bills at 2x once a request's input exceeds 272K tokens),",
    "contextWindow (tokens). null means 'no separate rate: bill as input'.",
    "Omitted values default by provider. claude: cachedInput 0.1x input, cacheWrite 1.25x input, cacheWriteLong 2x input, contextWindow 1000000.",
    "codex: cachedInput, cacheWrite and cacheWriteLong null, longContext false, contextWindow unknown.",
    "A copy named pricing.json in Foreman's data folder (Settings > Context & cost > Model prices) overrides this table without an app update:",
    "for each model, the entry from whichever file has the later pricingDate wins; models found in only one file are always used. Foreman reloads it on save."
